BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cmc-dmarc-sonic-arts-residency-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260805
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260806
SUMMARY:Deadline: CMC/DMARC Sonic Arts Residency 2026/2027
DESCRIPTION:The Digital Media and Arts Research Centre (DMARC) and CMC Irel
 and announce the second year of the Sonic Arts Residency Programme at the 
 University of Limerick Electronic Music Studio for 2026/27. The residency 
 offers Irish and international composers and sound artists an opportunity 
 to develop their creative practice and experiment using UL's facilities. F
 ACILITIES: the Electronic Music Studio (EMS) featuring both digital and an
 alogue workflows\, including a bespoke Buchla 200e\; a 32-channel immersiv
 e sound lab (SpADE)\; a makerspace supporting electronics and fabrication\
 ; and a range of well-equipped recording studios with a wide selection of 
 microphones and production hardware and software. DMARC is based in the Co
 mputer Science and Information Systems Department at UL and has a long his
 tory supporting digital arts\, electronic music\, and computer-aided compo
 sition (hosting the 2022 International Computer Music Conference and 2020 
 International Conference on Live Coding\, the Diffusion Prize with RTE Lyr
 ic FM\, and partnering with Light Moves Festival). PROGRAMME: each residen
 cy lasts 10 working days within one of two windows\, September-December 20
 26 or January-March 2027. Support includes a EUR 1\,000 honorarium from CM
 C\, a travel bursary up to EUR 350\, and an accommodation bursary up to EU
 R 1\,400 (ten nights)\, with DMARC helping identify accommodation. There i
 s an outreach/presentation element: a one-hour talk/performance for the DM
 ARC community of students and researchers\, and required documentation of 
 the process (photo\, video\, recordings\, and/or written reflections) that
  may be published by CMC on social media\; artists may also be invited to 
 contribute to CMC's amplify podcast series or online features at cmc.ie/fe
 atures. The programme runs 2025-27 with support for six artists (4 Irish\,
  2 international). ASSESSMENT: candidates apply via an online form submitt
 ing a CV\, work samples\, an outline of the residency project (including t
 echnical requirements)\, how they propose to engage with the facilities\, 
 and how the residency would benefit their practice. Criteria: artistic qua
 lity of the proposal including development of work using either the SpADE 
 system or Buchla 200e\; how the opportunity supports the candidate's curre
 nt career stage and artistic goals\; demonstrated technical capacity to en
 gage with the facilities\; and balanced representation of genres\, gender\
 , and geographical regions. TO APPLY: complete the online application form
  linked from the opportunity page. Closing date: 11am (IST)\, 5 August 202
 6\; late applications will not be accepted. Questions: jurgen.simpson@ul.i
 e or kfennell@cmc.ie. Applications are jointly assessed by DMARC and the C
 ontemporary Music Centre.\n\nOrganisation: Contemporary Music Centre (CMC)
  & Digital Media and Arts Research Centre (DMARC)\, University of Limerick
 \nLocation: University of Limerick\, Limerick\, Ireland (in person).\nAwar
 d: EUR 1\,000 honorarium (from CMC)\, plus a travel bursary up to EUR 350 
 and an accommodation bursary up to EUR 1\,400 (ten nights). No application
  fee.\nDuration: 10 working days\, scheduled within one of two windows: Se
 ptember-December 2026 or January-March 2027. Additional time may be reques
 ted where it does not incur extra cost.\n\nMore: http://cmc.ie/opportuniti
 es/open-call-cmcdmarc-sonic-arts-residency-20262027?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://cmc.ie/opportunities/open-call-cmcdmarc-sonic-arts-residency-202
 62027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:University of Limerick\, Limerick\, Ireland (in person).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondazione-prada-film-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260806
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260807
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondazione Prada Film Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fondazione Prada Film Fund is an annual initiative supporti
 ng independent cinema\, with an annual endowment of EUR 1.5 million backin
 g up to 14 feature film projects across development\, production\, and pos
 t-production. The Fund imposes NO restrictions on geography\, theme\, genr
 e\, or language and does not participate as a co-producer\, guaranteeing c
 omplete artistic freedom to filmmakers. It supports both established autho
 rs and new talents\, as well as research projects. SELECTION is based excl
 usively on quality\, originality\, vision\, and the strength and reliabili
 ty of the applicant structure\; projects are evaluated by independent read
 ers and external consultants\, with final selection and grant amounts dete
 rmined by a committee appointed by Fondazione Prada. ELIGIBILITY: applicat
 ions may be submitted only by a production company involved in the project
  (the applicant company remains solely responsible for meeting all require
 ments)\; open worldwide. DEADLINES (2026 call opened 30 June 2026): projec
 ts in production 6 August 2026\; projects in development and post-producti
 on 10 September 2026 (this card uses the earliest deadline). Post-producti
 on projects may submit a rough cut until 20 November 2026. Selected projec
 ts announced February 2027. Application documents are on the Fondazione Pr
 ada Film Fund page\; questions to filmfund@fondazioneprada.org.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Fondazione Prada\nLocation: Milan\, Italy-based fund\; open worldwi
 de to independent producers and production companies.\nAward: EUR 1.5 mill
 ion annual endowment supporting up to 14 projects. Individual grant amount
 s are set by the Fondazione Prada selection committee (no fixed per-stage 
 bands published). No application fee.\nDuration: Feature film funding (dev
 elopment\, production\, or post-production)\n\nMore: https://www.fondazion
 eprada.org/film-fund/?lang=en&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://www.fondazioneprada.org/film-fund/?lang=en&utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Milan\, Italy-based fund\; open worldwide to independent producers
  and production companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aixdesign-kb-national-library-ai-exhibition-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: AIxDESIGN x KB: Open Call for Sessions\, (Art)works and P
 erformances
DESCRIPTION:AIxDESIGN and the KB (Koninklijke Bibliotheek\, the National Li
 brary of the Netherlands) are building an exhibition and public programme 
 about AI\, made from the national collection\, at the KB in The Hague. Nad
 ia Piet is Creative Lead with the AIxDESIGN community\, co-presented with 
 the KB. The premise: long before neural nets\, libraries were the machines
  we built to organise human knowledge\, and the show uses the KB's collect
 ion to look at what AI is\, where it comes from\, and how it connects to t
 he older story of how we store\, sort\, and search what we know. Part of t
 he show lives in the KB Atelier\, with talks\, workshops\, and screenings 
 alongside\, intended as AI literacy you can wander into. WHAT THEY WANT: w
 ork that engages AI in some way (critical\, creative\, hands-on\, or playf
 ul)\; bonus if it also speaks to archives\, libraries\, or how we store an
 d sort knowledge\, though you do not need to touch the KB's collection to 
 take part. You may pitch to more than one track: (A) SOMETHING FOR THE OPE
 NING NIGHT\, a performance\, talk\, screening\, tour\, ritual\, booth\, ga
 me\, or other experience for the November 2026 opening\, fee EUR 1\,500 to
  2\,000\; (B) A SESSION IN THE EVENTS PROGRAMME\, a workshop or other sess
 ion once during the three-month run\, around 2.5 to 4 hours\, fee EUR 2\,0
 00 to 2\,500\; (C) AN (ART)WORK FOR THE EXHIBITION\, existing work in any 
 format (installation\, sculpture\, zine stand\, a corner of your own) stur
 dy enough for a public area with daily traffic\, honorarium EUR 200 to 400
  including licensing and production\; (D) SOMETHING ELSE ENTIRELY\, pitch 
 it anyway. WHO: artists\, designers\, researchers\, technologists\, perfor
 mers\, musicians\, archivists\, or educators working around AI\, data\, li
 braries\, or cultural heritage\; no finished idea or polished CV needed\, 
 just a clear\, specific pitch. You can be based anywhere and they especial
 ly welcome people outside the Netherlands\; the show is in-person in The H
 ague and the fee stays the same wherever you are coming from. HOW TO APPLY
 : send a short pitch through the form (which track\, your idea in a paragr
 aph or two\, roughly what it would need\, and a link to your work)\; takes
  about five minutes\, no full application required. Deadline: end of Augus
 t 2026. Questions to hello@aixdesign.co.\n\nOrganisation: AIxDESIGN\, co-p
 resented with the Koninklijke Bibliotheek (KB)\, National Library of the N
 etherlands\nLocation: KB\, The Hague\, Netherlands (in-person exhibition a
 nd programme)\; pitches welcome from people based anywhere\nAward: Fees by
  track: opening-night experience EUR 1\,500 to 2\,000\; a session in the e
 vents programme EUR 2\,000 to 2\,500\; an existing (art)work for the exhib
 ition EUR 200 to 400 honorarium (including licensing and production). The 
 fee stays the same wherever you are based.\nDuration: Exhibition runs Nove
 mber 2026 to February 2027\; opening event November 2026\n\nMore: https://
 nadiapiet.notion.site/Open-Call-AIxDESIGN-x-KB-Sessions-Art-works-More-38f
 37d0038338102b128c57cbeb16d2d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
