UID:stimuleringsfonds-fresh-perspectives-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Fresh Perspectives 2026
DESCRIPTION:Open call from the Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfon
 ds) for cross-sector collaboration projects that offer new perspectives on
  current challenges such as climate\, housing\, polarisation\, migration o
 r inequality of opportunity. The procedure runs in two phases. In Phase 1\
 , the applicant and partner use the period to prepare and kick off the pro
 ject\, further explore the theme\, intended end product and collaboration\
 , and investigate possibilities (including working on a prototype or proof
  of concept)\, concluding with a project plan\, budget and collaboration a
 greement. Phase 2\, open only to projects selected and fully completed in 
 Phase 1\, focuses on implementation and requires both a written applicatio
 n and a presentation to the advisory committee\; projects may deliver vari
 ous end products (an activity\, intervention\, event\, publication\, servi
 ce\, product or process) accompanied by a suitable form of knowledge shari
 ng such as a presentation\, symposium or publication. ELIGIBILITY: applica
 nts working with at least one partner in cross-sector collaboration\; see 
 the fund's open-call page for full eligibility details. The Phase 1 applic
 ation window runs from 19 May 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 25 August 2026\, 16:00 
 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Ind
 ustries Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands (Dutch fund\; cross-sector collabo
 ration)\nAward: Two-phase grant. Phase 1: ten grants of EUR 10\,000 (max 5
  months\, startup 1 December 2026 to 30 April 2027) to prepare\, explore a
 nd prototype the project. Phase 2: ten grants of EUR 50\,000 (max 12 month
 s\, implementation 1 September 2027 to 31 August 2028) for projects select
 ed and fully completed in Phase 1. No application fee.\nDuration: Phase 1 
 max 5 months\; Phase 2 (if selected) max 12 months\n\nMore: https://www.st
 imuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-fresh-perspectives-2026?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-fresh-perspectives
 -2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (Dutch fund\; cross-sector collaboration)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Foundation: Fellowship 2027-2028
DESCRIPTION:Founded by the artist and philanthropist Jerome Hill\, the Cama
 rgo Foundation has run this residency in Cassis on the Mediterranean coast
  since 1971\, and more than 1\,500 fellows have been through it. Fourteen 
 fellowships are awarded per cycle\, split roughly seven artists and seven 
 scholars or thinkers\, which is the point: the interdisciplinary cohort is
  the programme\, not a side effect. IMPORTANT: the Foundation has stated t
 hat this is the FINAL fellowship awarded through a public open call before
  it moves to a new selection process from 2027\, so if you have been meani
 ng to apply\, this is the cycle. RESEARCH\, NOT PRODUCTION: this is delibe
 rately structured as a research residency. You propose a project or line o
 f inquiry\, which can be development of a new work\, research preceding fu
 ture creative work\, or a broader investigation in your practice. Visual a
 rtists are explicitly reminded that research is prioritised over productio
 n\, and the Foundation supplies no art materials\, technical equipment or 
 artwork shipping\, so anything needing extensive fabrication is a poor fit
 . Fellows lead one resident session built around their own research or met
 hodology\, and attendance at these sessions is mandatory for everyone. Opt
 ional public Open Studios and introductions to organisations across the Ai
 x-Marseille-Provence region are also part of it. ELIGIBILITY: professional
  artists\, scholars and thinkers of any nationality. Artists should have a
 t least five years of professional practice and a mature body of work evid
 enced by exhibitions\, performances\, publications\, awards or grants. Per
 formance artists\, theatre directors\, choreographers\, multidisciplinary 
 artists\, writers\, filmmakers\, composers and visual artists are all elig
 ible within their categories. Collaborative applications of up to three me
 mbers are accepted. APPLICATION: four separate written responses covering 
 the project\, the research questions\, why Camargo specifically\, and why 
 now in your career\; reviewers are reading for a coherent research traject
 ory rather than a production proposal. An applicant webinar runs 1 Septemb
 er 2026. Deadline 1 October 2026 at 17:59 EST / 23:59 CET\; notifications 
 April 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Fondation Camargo\nLocation: Cassis\, France 
 (Mediterranean coast)\nAward: EUR 3\,500 stipend (EUR 350 per week for 10 
 weeks)\, basic transportation to and from Cassis\, a furnished apartment o
 n campus\, and a studio or appropriate workspace\, plus a reference librar
 y\, music and conference room and open-air theatre. Art materials\, techni
 cal equipment and shipping of artworks are NOT provided. No application fe
 e listed.\nDuration: Ten weeks. Fall 2027 session: 8 September to 17 Novem
 ber 2027. Spring 2028 session: 23 February to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https:/
 /camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cassis\, France (Mediterranean coast)
END:VEVENT
