BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movida-labs-dance-technology-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: MOVIDA: Labs on Dance and Technology 2026/27
DESCRIPTION:MOVIDA is a Creative Europe co-funded consortium pairing academ
 ic institutions with dance centres across four European cities. Sixteen du
 os\, each made up of one dancer and one creative technologist\, are select
 ed across four themed labs: AI and accessibility in Bucharest\, AI and AR/
 VR in Dusseldorf\, AI and robotics in Lisbon\, and AI and mental health in
  Tallinn. Applicants are assessed on demonstrated capability in integratin
 g technology with live performance\, computational creativity\, and audien
 ce interaction. Participants selected for the labs receive fast-track cons
 ideration for the MOVIDA residencies running in 2027 and 2028.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: MOVIDA (Movement and Virtual Intelligence for the Development and Ac
 cessibility of Artists and Audiences)\nLocation: Four labs across Europe: 
 Bucharest (Romania)\, Dusseldorf (Germany)\, Lisbon and Montemor-o-Novo (P
 ortugal)\, and Tallinn (Estonia). Applications are accepted only from duos
  of one dancer and one creative technologist\; you cannot apply solo. Both
  members must reside in an EU or Creative Europe eligible country\, so Net
 herlands-based applicants qualify.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 gross per artist (EU
 R 2\,400 per duo)\, plus travel and accommodation covered\, plus a product
 ion budget of up to EUR 500 per duo. Accessibility and personal-assistance
  costs are covered by separate agreement. No application fee.\nDuration: N
 ine days per lab\, scheduled between 3 December 2026 and 11 February 2027\
 n\nMore: https://movida.dance/news/call-labs/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://movida.dance/news/call-labs/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Four labs across Europe: Bucharest (Romania)\, Dusseldorf (Germany
 )\, Lisbon and Montemor-o-Novo (Portugal)\, and Tallinn (Estonia). Applica
 tions are accepted only from duos of one dancer and one creative technolog
 ist\; you cannot apply solo. Both members must reside in an EU or Creative
  Europe eligible country\, so Netherlands-based applicants qualify.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:francoise-cite-internationale-arts-clinique-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Association Francoise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine x Cite 
 internationale des arts: Research and Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Launched in 2025\, this research and creation residency explore
 s the links between contemporary art\, psychiatry and the human sciences. 
 It is expressly not a therapeutic programme. It seeks artists whose practi
 ce resonates with the notion of the clinical\, meaning a situated approach
  that works closely with lived narratives and specific contexts\, and that
  engages with questions of care. The selected artist receives tailored sup
 port from Albertine de Galbert\, a clinical psychologist and exhibition cu
 rator\, including four to six working sessions\, alongside networking and 
 meeting time with programme partners. Outputs include an ongoing online jo
 urnal\, a mid-residency open studio\, and a closing presentation (exhibiti
 on\, public talk or publication) defined with the artist. Applications go 
 by email as a single PDF of no more than 15 MB to residence@francoiseartme
 mo.fr\, and require a two-page CV\, a ten-page portfolio\, a two-page stat
 ement of intent\, and a letter of recommendation from an institution or a 
 curator. A jury of four to six art and psychiatry specialists decides\, wi
 th results announced in September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Association Franc
 oise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine / Cite internationale des arts\nLocation:
  Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). Open to
  artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career or esta
 blished\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working in Fre
 nch or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current accessibil
 ity standards for people with disabilities.\nAward: Grant of EUR 1\,000 ne
 t of tax per month\, plus a furnished studio-apartment (20 to 35 sq m\, co
 mbining living and working space)\, international return travel to Paris a
 irports or stations\, travel insurance\, and capped research support again
 st receipts. Additional fees apply for accompanying persons. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Approximately 12 weeks\, 5 January to 26 March 2027\n\nM
 ore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associa
 tion-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associati
 on-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). 
 Open to artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career 
 or established\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working
  in French or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current acc
 essibility standards for people with disabilities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:klang-copenhagen-open-call-2027-music-movement@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Klang Copenhagen Avantgarde Music Festival: Open Call 202
 7\, MUSIC/MOVEMENT
DESCRIPTION:Klang\, Copenhagen's avantgarde music festival\, is seeking one
  to three projects at the intersection of experimental music and movement\
 , dance or choreography for its 2027 edition at Dansehallerne. Important c
 onstraint: the call is explicitly for ready-to-go projects\, not commissio
 ns or works in progress\, so the work must already be finished and product
 ion-ready. Submission is a one-page PDF covering artistic description\, bu
 dget overview\, bios\, duration and media links\, emailed to opencall@klan
 g.dk with 'Open Call 2027' in the subject line. The submission window runs
  1 July to 1 September 2026. The toaspern|moeller duo together with Klang 
 Festival review feasible submissions in September 2026\, with notification
  in October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Klang - Copenhagen Avantgarde Music Fes
 tival\nLocation: Dansehallerne\, Copenhagen\, Denmark. No nationality\, ag
 e or education restrictions are stated on the call page.\nAward: Klang aim
 s to cover production costs and performer fees. Travel and accommodation a
 re discussed case by case rather than guaranteed. No commission fee is off
 ered\, since the call seeks finished work rather than new creation. No app
 lication fee.\nDuration: Performance during Klang Festival 2027\, provisio
 nal dates 15 to 18 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.klang.dk/open-calls/open
 call2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.klang.dk/open-calls/opencall2027?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dansehallerne\, Copenhagen\, Denmark. No nationality\, age or educ
 ation restrictions are stated on the call page.
END:VEVENT
